# BEQ Corpus Release Audit

Audit date: 2026-08-12

## Proof upgrades completed before release

The Tilting, Rungs, BEQ Loop, technical MTT--BEQ interface, and interpretive
integration papers were reopened for proof upgrades or propagation before
publication. Tilting now contains the
conditional quantum-substrate necessity theorem and the finite-sample
functional-necessity certificate. Rungs now contains the exact
multi-rung Dobrushin contraction bound. The BEQ Loop now contains the exact
binary selection--transmission identity and the exact quantum-to-heredity
mediation product. The technical interface now contains the robust
model-separation theorem. The interpretive synthesis now explains that theorem's
strict uncertainty-gap consequence without duplicating it.

A final prepublication pass tightened three points without changing the result
tier: substrate stability is explicitly necessary rather than sufficient for
life; the Dobrushin contrast diagnostic now propagates simultaneous confidence
bounds; and the MTT--BEQ separation theorem now defines the empirical estimator
and its compatibility test explicitly.

## Verdict

The eight-paper BEQ corpus is internally coherent at its declared evidence
tiers. Each paper has a reviewed TeX source, generated Markdown, compiled PDF,
paper-specific revision audit, release metadata, and a public Zenodo record.
All eight public records match the reviewed local title, version, description,
PDF checksum, file size, references, concept lineage, and BEQ community state.

The corpus does not establish a universal quantum contribution to biology,
free will, a completed MTT-to-biology derivation, or the prevalence of life.
Those former inferences have been removed or retained only as explicitly
withdrawn claims. The corrected corpus is a research program with exact
statistical and interface results, system-specific physical evidence, and
clearly marked biological hypotheses.

